{
  "claimable": false,
  "schema_version": 1,
  "name": "cloudevents",
  "description": "CloudEvents v1.0 export conformance. `envelope_cases` pin the projection of an audit event onto a CloudEvents envelope AND its canonical string form, which must be byte-identical across SDKs - the string is the contract, the parsed envelope is carried alongside it so a reader can see the shape without decoding. The mapping choices worth knowing: (source, id) is the audit chain coordinate (sdk_session_id, seq_no), so a sink that dedupes CloudEvents dedupes on the same identity the ledger does; an event with no chain position falls back to request_id and says so rather than generating an id that would make every re-export look new; dataschema is a URN because an https URL would promise something is served there. `time_cases` pin the RFC 3339 formatter on its own, including the inputs where the two runtimes' built-in formatters disagree, which is why each SDK spells the format out instead of calling toISOString / isoformat. Harnesses: sdk-typescript/tests/unit/cloudevents-conformance.test.ts, sdk-python/tests/test_cloudevents_conformance.py.",
